Statement of modifications, as required by Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b):

1. model/model_minimind.py — added looped execution of the shared block stack:
   - `n_loops` config field (default 1 = upstream behaviour, unchanged code path)
   - per-round residual gates (`loop_gates`), initialised to 1/sqrt(T) (LayerScale style)
   - input re-injection of the first-round embedding on rounds r > 0
   - KV cache automatically disabled when n_loops > 1 (a single cache slot cannot
     represent several passes of the same layers; looping therefore does not save VRAM)
2. trainer/train_pretrain.py, trainer/train_full_sft.py, trainer/train_dpo.py,
   trainer/train_grpo.py, trainer/train_agent.py, eval_llm.py, scripts/eval_toolcall.py —
   added a `--n_loops` flag (default 1) and pass it through to the model config.
3. Added scripts/eval_math_toolcall.py — a 20-question math tool-use benchmark with
   embedded questions and automatic grading (upstream's eval_toolcall.py only prints
   demo outputs and does not score).
4. Added scripts/make_report_figs.py — generates the figures shipped in figures/.
5. Added docs/, figures/, README.md, README_en.md describing the looped-vs-baseline
   A/B experiment run on top of upstream MiniMind.

Unmodified: dataset pipeline and formats, tokenizer, training loop structure, and the
MoE / LoRA / distillation features of the upstream project.

